.nh
.TH "PB-MACHINE-TAG" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-machine-tag - Show or change a machine's tags


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb machine tag <machine> [add|remove|set] [tag...] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show a machine's tags, or change them in the active workspace's policy: add
or remove tags, or set the full list. Tags are tag:<name> (the tag: prefix may be
left out). A tag that does not exist yet is created; a tag left with no machines
is removed unless a rule uses it. A change that gives or takes anyone's access
(rules on the tag) is printed and must be confirmed; --yes confirms it. Members
may tag only machines they shared.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for tag

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	confirm the printed access changes without asking


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb machine tag db
  pb machine tag db add prod ci
  pb machine tag db remove ci --yes
  pb machine tag db set prod
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-machine(1)\fP
